{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792777069,"nonce":"TKkI8DC65/yuKB+wAiAj50sEcCk=","title":"zynml: const_generics_lower expects generic templates in the lowered module","message":"`cargo test -p zynml --test const_generics_lower` fails with \"function `make` should be lowered\" (const_param_reaches_hir_signature), and CI's native tests job has stopped there on Linux, macOS and Windows since 10-22. The job ends at the first failing test binary, so the Python and Lua suites after it never run in CI.\n\nBisected on the NUC: first bad commit 122d0cee \"TypeScript: specialize generic functions through shared HIR\". `monomorphize_module` now removes every generic template from the module and keeps only concrete instances, so a test that lowers through `ZyntaxRuntime::lower_typed_program` (which monomorphizes) and looks for the uninstantiated `make` finds nothing. The test checks the declaration half of const generics: it needs the module before specialization.","files":null}]}